{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1507368-how-do-acolytes-become-acolytes","id":1507368,"title":"How do Acolytes become Acolytes?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-04-03T21:05:28-07:00","id":1507368,"title":"How do Acolytes become Acolytes?","content":"I havent found any info about this or any protocol/procedure, not even in Ascension's Right Hand. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5394-argonot","name":"Argonot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-03T22:44:27-07:00","id":1507375,"title":"","content":"By definition, an &quot;Acolyte&quot; is merely someone who assists or serves a Mage in some capacity. They are ordinary people without any special knowledge, skill, or power. They may not even know the person they are helping is a Mage. I think most Acolytes come by their roles naturally.<br /> <br /> Does the Mage own some kind of bookstore? The people who work there (her employees) are Acolytes. Does the Mage own some kind of house, mansion, apartment, office, etc. that requires cleaners, servants, personal assistants, secretaries, etc. that perform personal tasks for the Mage? Those are Acolytes. Does the Mage participate and run some kind of group, whether it is a Bible study group, church or cult, self-help seminar, hobby organization, etc.? While the regular membership may not be Acolytes, anyone who helps the Mage run the organization would be. For some Acolytes, the Mage might even be their &quot;customer&quot;. For example, if a Mage routinely visits a research library, one of the librarians may take a liking to her and begin actively helping her out in her research as part of her capacity of working at the library. Many things would count.<br /> <br /> I think perhaps only gradually might an Acolyte figure out their employer, leader, friend, etc. is involved in the supernatural.<br /> <br /> In many cases, they are similar to supporting casts of superheroes. Aunt May, Alfred Pennyworth, Edwin Jarvis, Rick Jones, Foggy Nelson, and Jimmy Olsen would all be Acolytes. (More powerful characters that only help the superhero out occasionally would probably be more like Allies than Acolytes like Ben Urich, Robbie Robertson, Commissioner Gordon, and Emil Hamilton.)<br /> <br /> It all depends on how the Mage interacts with people.<br /> <br /> Of course there are exceptions to this. If the Mage rescues someone from a supernatural threat, that person might agree to serve them in gratitude. And there are many other scenarios that would result in someone becoming an Acolyte with full knowledge the person is a Mage or somehow special.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0gU_NqsoOE0\" data-code=\"0gU_NqsoOE0\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/0gU_NqsoOE0/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> I think once you figure out how the Mage character lives and who they interact with, you can quickly assign which other NPCs are her Acolytes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-04T02:36:49-07:00","id":1507386,"title":"","content":"That feels like an overly broad definition to me. Acolytes in the books don't just mean people in your mage's regular life. They're people that know that magic is real even if they don't have any juice of their own. Acolytes generally don't count as Sleepers (or at least aren't Sleepers to a broad grouping of mages, unlike cultists that are more dedicated to a specific magical outlook). Acolytes aren't just aware of the supernatural, they're capable of being active assistants to mages in magical efforts. <br /> <br /> Like, Aunt May (in her most common presentations though I admit this is less so in some of the more popular recent ones) wouldn't be an acolyte because she's just Peter's parental figure. She doesn't know he's Spider-man or actively assist him like that. Alfred is a much better example of what the books tend to portrayal as an acolyte: He knows Bruce is Batman, and he's an active support figure in both sides of Bruce's life. He's bought into the Batman cause to the point of being able and willing to operate the Batcave to assist Batman while he's out in the field. In various continuities he's even faked being Batman well enough to help hide Bruce's identity. Alfred might not be a superhero, but he's part of the Bat-team.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-05T05:43:00-07:00","id":1507475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Argonot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1507368-how-do-acolytes-become-acolytes#post1507368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I havent found any info about this or any protocol/procedure, not even in Ascension's Right Hand.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say that some - if not all or most - Acolytes and Consors get a mystical or supernatural intiation or start, usually through some event or ceremony.<br /> <br /> Such rites and events might be comparable between groups of same or simillar Mages. For example there should be some commonility in regard to these in teams and groups consisting mainly or exclusively of Tradition Mages ( Wizards ), or Nephandi Mages ( Warlocks ), or Solificati, or Templar Knights, or Technocrats ( Enlightened Scientists ) . I mean the Technicians and the Extraordinary Citizens in regard to Technocrats, of course.<br /> <br /> Acolytes and Consors also most likely partake regularly in magical or supernatural tasks and events to bolster, understand. and develop the philosophical, mystical, practical, mundane, and cultural sections, parts, and areas of who they are and what they do in regard to their beliefs and ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 04-05-2023, 08:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-09T20:55:45-07:00","id":1507917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1507368-how-do-acolytes-become-acolytes?p=1507386#post1507386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That feels like an overly broad definition to me. Acolytes in the books don't just mean people in your mage's regular life. They're people that know that magic is real even if they don't have any juice of their own. Acolytes generally don't count as Sleepers (or at least aren't Sleepers to a broad grouping of mages, unlike cultists that are more dedicated to a specific magical outlook). Acolytes aren't just aware of the supernatural, they're capable of being active assistants to mages in magical efforts.<br /> <br /> Like, Aunt May (in her most common presentations though I admit this is less so in some of the more popular recent ones) wouldn't be an acolyte because she's just Peter's parental figure. She doesn't know he's Spider-man or actively assist him like that. Alfred is a much better example of what the books tend to portrayal as an acolyte: He knows Bruce is Batman, and he's an active support figure in both sides of Bruce's life. He's bought into the Batman cause to the point of being able and willing to operate the Batcave to assist Batman while he's out in the field. In various continuities he's even faked being Batman well enough to help hide Bruce's identity. Alfred might not be a superhero, but he's part of the Bat-team.</div> </div> </div> </div>^This.<br /> <br /> While &quot;Acolyte&quot; isn't a Background, to my knowledge, there are plenty of actual Backgrounds that cover various sorts of &quot;helpers&quot; a Mage can call upon. I don't think an Acolyte is really a Retainer or Contact, which is what many mundane examples come out to be. Acolytes are more like Allies. Folks who know at least something of a Mage's &quot;lifestyle&quot;, and is willing to help for a variety of reasons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-09T21:09:27-07:00","id":1507919,"title":"","content":"Some of that is just that certain Backgrounds can overlap a bit more than the dots represent well. Alfred being an example of this too: he qualifies as an Ally, Mentor, and Retainer (to varying degrees for such a long standing character). He's ex-special forces with far more skills than his status as the Wayne family butler would imply (Ally), but he's also a butler (Retainer), and he's put his own past training and and his status as a surrogate father figure to help guide Bruce (Mentor).<br /> <br /> One of the Mage Rev. books had a good sidebar on letting players stack multiple Backgrounds/Merits/Flaws on one NPC. From a narrative standpoint it makes sense not to have NPCs defined so neatly, and from a game-play perspective &quot;all the eggs in one basket&quot; is as much of a risk as it is a benefit. You get one really powerful NPC for all that investment, but it also means one NPC to neutralize to deny you a lot of benefits as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}